  "claim": "During the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl on December 19, 2009, future Atlanta Falcons wide receiver Mohamed Sanu Sr was the game's MVP.",
  "evidencia": "Page: 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl. Sentence: The 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl presented by Beef 'O' Brady's, formerly known as the St. Petersburg Bowl, was the second edition of the college football bowl game and was played at Tropicana Field in St. Petersburg, Florida.\nPage: 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl. Sentence: Rutgers defeated UCF 45–24 in a game where Mohamed Sanu, the game's MVP, caught 4 passes for 97 yards and a touchdown in addition to rushing 14 times for 47 yards and two touchdowns.\nPage: Mohamed Sanu. Sentence: Mohamed Sanu Sr. (born August 22, 1989) is an American football wide receiver for the Atlanta Falcons of the National Football League (NFL).",
