        "original_id": "ef54e666-fc84-5c05-b519-bb978f80dd6d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl\n- People: Mohamed Sanu\n- Organizations: Rutgers, UCF, Atlanta Falcons, NFL\n- Places: Tropicana Field, St. Petersburg, Florida\n\nFacts:\n- The 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl presented by Beef 'O' Brady's was the second edition of the college football bowl game.\n- The 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl was played at Tropicana Field in St. Petersburg, Florida.\n- Rutgers defeated UCF 45–24 in the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl.\n- Mohamed Sanu was the MVP of the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl.\n- In the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl, Mohamed Sanu caught 4 passes for 97 yards and a touchdown and rushed 14 times for 47 yards and two touchdowns.\n- Mohamed Sanu Sr., born August 22, 1989, is an American football wide receiver for the Atlanta Falcons of the National Football League.",
